[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/963","id":4239821596,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc78tosc","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/963","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/963.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/963.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/963","number":963,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: deterministic content validation and quality report for generated documents","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nPhase 1 of the multi-stage resume pipeline programme: every generated résumé and cover letter is now **deterministically validated against the candidate's own source document**, with the result persisted, surfaced in the UI, and available to the agent. The core rule made mechanical: the LLM decides HOW to present verified evidence — these validators catch it deciding WHAT.\n\n- **`validate/content/`** (L1): 25-code deterministic validator family — factual (unsourced metrics/terms/dates, dropped roles, altered project links), alignment (coverage regression vs source, missing evidenced requirements), consistency (dates, title drift, skills claimed-but-not-demonstrated, project-structure tiers), duplicates, ATS structure + keyword-density, and a `voice.*` anti-AI-tell family (single-source lexicon shared with the generation prompts via codegen). Criticals come only from deterministic checks — a model can never emit one.\n- **`documents/evidence.rs`** (L1): evidence extraction (`extract_evidence`/`rank_bullets`) — the `rank_trim_candidates` core moved out of the R8-frozen `match_resume.rs` (net −141 lines, trim-panel wire-compat pinned by test).\n- **`quality_report` on `ai_generations`** (ADR-007 §F2): opaque wrapper JSON, per-top-level-key merge, full backup/restore round-trip, 256 KB clamps on both write paths.\n- **`resume:validateContent` IPC** (5-step): server-side clamps, strict docKind, content-free spans (ADR-027).\n- **Four agent Read tools**: `validate_resume`, `search_candidate_evidence`, `lookup_salary`, `get_trim_suggestions` — fenced, clamped, least-privilege-pinned; fence-tag registry + `tool_result` marker hardened against forgery (incl. nested-marker bypass).\n- **`pnpm gen:prompts` codegen**: the anti-AI-tell lexicon is generated from `natural-voice.ts` into Rust with a CI drift gate — one source instructs the model and validates its output, guarded in both directions.\n- **Renderer**: integrity badge + QualityReportPanel (evidence-first, guidance-framed, en+de), report-carrying saves, staleness via source-text hash, Re-check action, hand-edit nudge.\n\n## Review trail\n\nFive domain critics + a security review + a 3-pass `/review` ensemble with per-finding fresh-context verification ran before this PR. Every blocking finding was fixed with mutation-verified regression tests, including: six false-positive Criticals on truthful documents, a per-key merge defect, a forged-fence-tag hole, a renderer cancel race, a UTF-8 boundary panic on accented URLs (`café-berlin.de`) that would have aborted the app mid-generation, and a malformed-persisted-report renderer crash. Zero verifier-rejected findings; ledger updated.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo test --lib`: 3410 passed · `--test architecture`: 18/18 · clippy `-D warnings` clean\n- Desktop vitest: 3074 passed · prompts 742 · workspace typecheck 13/13 · `lint:strict` clean\n- `gen:ipc:check` + `gen:prompts:check` clean · backup/export round-trip covers the new column\n- Fixtures include paraphrased-but-truthful en+de documents (zero-Critical guards) and accented-URL project entries\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-08-09T19:09:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T04:06:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7d56e43fb04405c365abee90e836519557276198","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10964600421,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACjYqGZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Documentation and markdown"},{"id":11212541200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/desktop","name":"app/desktop","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/desktop"},{"id":11212541282,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/shared","name":"pkg/shared","color":"1abc9c","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/shared"},{"id":11212541380,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNxA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/prompts","name":"pkg/prompts","color":"2bbbad","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/prompts"},{"id":11212541489,"node_id":"